    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSherry FitzGerald Farrell are delighted, under joint agency, to present to the market the distinguished Breanross House, the former Estate Manager's residence of the historic Lough Rynn Estate.\n\nThis enchanting period home, dating from circa 1840, exudes timeless character and charm, offering a rare opportunity to acquire a landmark property of significant heritage and scale.\n\nTucked away approximately 2 km from Mohill town and the N4, Breanross House is approached via a sweeping private avenue of approximately 700 metres, opening to reveal a gracious residence set amidst tranquil surroundings on an elevated site of circa 1 acre.\n\nSteeped in history, this remarkable home was originally commissioned by the Clement family — notable landowners who, during the 19th century, held extensive estates throughout Ireland, at one time encompassing more than 100,000 acres.\n\nBeyond its handsome façade, Breanross House extends to an impressive c.490m sq., thoughtfully enhanced and sympathetically extended over time to provide a substantial and versatile home. The ground floor boasts three elegant reception rooms, a grand entrance hall with feature staircase, and a bespoke bar area within the principal reception room — ideal for entertaining in style. A large commercial-grade kitchen with adjoining storeroom caters for both domestic and professional use, while a charming dining area occupies the original cottage wing, complemented by ladies' and gents' WCs and additional storage.\n\nTo the rear lies a self-contained owner's quarters, comprising a spacious kitchen/living room, utility area, and private staircase, offering both privacy and flexibility.\n\nThe first floor provides eight bedrooms in total, four of which are en suite, including a wheelchair-accessible wet room. The remaining four bedrooms are served by well-appointed bathrooms, while a large linen/plant room adds valuable functionality.\n\nThe property is fully fire compliant, with a modern fire detection system and fire doors throughout. Services include a private well water supply, septic tank, and extensive rainwater storage of approximately 40,000 litres via three underground tanks. Heating is provided by oil-fired central heating, thoughtfully supplemented by solar panels for enhanced efficiency.\n\nOffering immense potential, Breanross House lends itself beautifully to a variety of uses — from a magnificent private residence to a charming boutique guesthouse or B&B.\nWith its rich history, graceful proportions, and secluded setting, this is a truly exceptional opportunity to acquire one of the region's most distinctive period homes."
      },
